# Docker build context for the ingest image (deploy/ingest.Dockerfile). An allowlist, like
# /.dockerignore: everything is excluded, then only what the image is built from is let back
# in. Docker uses this file instead of /.dockerignore for that Dockerfile, so the web image's
# context is unchanged.
#
# Never in the context: generated releases and the store (var/), v1's own files that hold
# FRED- and Yahoo-sourced values (data/, dist/, web/, .git), the fixtures, and v1's
# hand-entered tables inside the atlas package (the four .yaml files; the ingest job publishes
# from the store and never runs the legacy converter). The Catalog (catalog/) is let in: it
# names Series and their Sources and holds no value. So is content/ (M26; ADR 0033, ADR 0040):
# the Events, Claims, Topics and headline list a Release is compiled from, and the Claim locks
# committed for the public Profile, which are in the repository only where the register
# allows redistribution. Without it the timer's Releases would hold no Event and no Claim.
# User notes (notes/) are not content and stay out. tests/v2/test_ignore_rules.py checks this
# file, and deploy/check-images.sh checks the built image holds exactly the tracked content
# files. Do not add the paths above here (build protocol, point 7).
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!atlas
!schema
!catalog
!checks/spot.json
!content
!packages/core/package.json
!packages/core/bin
!packages/core/src

atlas/approval.yaml
atlas/catalog.yaml
atlas/events.yaml
atlas/politics.yaml
**/__pycache__
**/.DS_Store
**/*.test.ts
packages/core/src/testing.ts
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.local
